{"alignment":[{"from":["d1:REQ-1","d2:REQ-1","d3:REQ-1"],"mergedReq":"REQ-1"},{"from":["d1:REQ-2","d2:REQ-1","d3:REQ-1"],"mergedReq":"REQ-2"},{"from":["d1:REQ-3","d2:REQ-1","d3:REQ-1"],"mergedReq":"REQ-3"},{"from":["d1:REQ-4","d2:REQ-2","d3:REQ-2"],"mergedReq":"REQ-4"},{"from":["d1:REQ-5","d2:REQ-4","d3:REQ-3"],"mergedReq":"REQ-5"},{"from":["d1:REQ-6","d2:REQ-5","d3:REQ-4"],"mergedReq":"REQ-6"},{"from":["d1:REQ-7","d2:REQ-3","d3:REQ-12"],"mergedReq":"REQ-7"},{"from":["d1:REQ-8","d2:REQ-6","d3:REQ-5"],"mergedReq":"REQ-8"},{"from":["d1:REQ-9","d2:REQ-7","d3:REQ-6"],"mergedReq":"REQ-9"},{"from":["d1:REQ-9"],"mergedReq":"REQ-10"},{"from":["d1:REQ-10","d2:REQ-8","d3:REQ-7"],"mergedReq":"REQ-11"},{"from":["d1:REQ-11","d2:REQ-9","d3:REQ-8"],"mergedReq":"REQ-12"},{"from":["d1:REQ-12","d2:REQ-10","d3:REQ-9"],"mergedReq":"REQ-13"},{"from":["d1:REQ-12","d2:REQ-11","d3:REQ-9"],"mergedReq":"REQ-14"},{"from":["d1:REQ-13","d2:REQ-12","d3:REQ-10"],"mergedReq":"REQ-15"},{"from":["d1:REQ-14","d2:REQ-13","d3:REQ-11","d3:REQ-7"],"mergedReq":"REQ-16"},{"from":["d1:REQ-15","d2:REQ-14","d3:REQ-13"],"mergedReq":"REQ-17"},{"from":["d1:REQ-16","d2:REQ-15","d3:REQ-14"],"mergedReq":"REQ-18"},{"from":["d1:REQ-16"],"mergedReq":"REQ-19"},{"from":["d2:REQ-15","d3:REQ-14"],"mergedReq":"REQ-20"}],"conflicts":["Invoice detail screen 'Send reminder' button: d1:REQ-16 shows it only while the invoice is overdue (hidden for paid invoices) → merged REQ-19; d2:REQ-15 and d3:REQ-14 show the button with no overdue condition, and d2's notes say the detail screen may show it for any invoice → merged REQ-20. On the server side only d1 (REQ-9 → merged REQ-10) rejects sends for invoices that aren't overdue; d2 and d3 leave this open. The client must decide.","Overdue list performance sizing: d1 NFR-1 measures at 10,000 invoices / 1,000 customers (merged NFR-1), while d2 NFR-1 and d3 NFR-1 measure at 5,000 open invoices / 500 customers (merged NFR-2).","Send-reminder timing: d1 NFR-2 sets a provider timeout of ≤ 8 s and a 10 s maximum response (merged NFR-3); d2 NFR-2 sets a 10 s timeout and a 12 s maximum (merged NFR-4); d3 NFR-2 sets a 10 s timeout and p95 ≤ 5 s (merged NFR-5)."],"spec":{"assumptions":["ASM-1 (high risk): invoices, customers, the paid/closed status and the customer email field already exist in the client's .NET 8 API and Postgres database and are read from there. No repository was available, so every requirement is ADDED and all endpoint paths and field names (e.g. GET /api/overdue-invoices or /api/invoices/overdue, GET /api/invoices/{id}, POST /api/invoices/{id}/reminders, POST /api/email-events or /api/email-provider/events) are placeholders to be mapped to the real API.","Days-overdue buckets: ASM-5 (7–30/31–60/61–90/90+) is used over ASM-14 (7–14/15–30/30+), with the top bucket starting at 91 so buckets don't overlap. The client must confirm.","Email channel: ASM-6 (transactional provider with signed bounce webhooks) is used over ASM-12 (existing SMTP relay), because Q-8 needs bounces reported back and a plain SMTP relay can't reliably do that. The client must confirm.","Email template: the wording and from address come from a configured template; ASM-8 (client provides wording) and ASM-15 (we draft, client approves) are combined. The body must contain invoice number, amount and due date.","The overdue threshold is an app setting with default 7 (ASM-3/ASM-10). Today's date comes from a configured business timezone (ASM-9/ASM-11). Days overdue counts whole calendar days from the due date (ASM-4), so an invoice first appears on the list with days overdue = 7.","The double-submit window is 60 seconds, checked per invoice on the server (ASM-13), counting from the previous accepted request that reached the provider, whatever the provider outcome. Duplicates rejected this way are not recorded in reminder history.","Requests blocked before any provider call (missing email, not overdue, duplicate, unauthenticated) are not delivery attempts and create no reminder history entry; Q-3's 'every attempt' is read as every attempt that reaches the provider.","The provider gives each send a message id that is stored on the reminder history entry and used to match bounce events; the webhook is authenticated by the provider's signature against a configured secret, not by staff authentication.","The sender recorded in history is the identity of the authenticated user from the existing API authentication.","Error status codes (400, 401, 404, 409, 422, 502) are proposals; the client API's own error conventions take priority if they differ.","Reminder history is shown newest first. Reminders can be sent from both the overdue list and the invoice detail screen (ASM-16)."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 response time ≤ 1000 ms with 10,000 invoices and 1,000 customers in the database, with or without filters","text":"The overdue list endpoint responds quickly at the expected data size, with or without filters (d1 sizing)."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"p95 response time ≤ 1000 ms with 5,000 open invoices and 500 customers","text":"The overdue list endpoint responds quickly at the expected data size, with or without filters (d2/d3 sizing)."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"Endpoint returns within 10 s in 100% of calls; provider call timeout ≤ 8 s","text":"The send-reminder endpoint gives the staff user a result within a fixed time, including when the provider is slow (d1 reading)."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"Provider call timeout 10 s; endpoint returns within 12 s in 100% of requests","text":"The send-reminder endpoint does not hang on a slow email provider (d2 reading)."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"p95 ≤ 5 s; provider call timeout 10 s, after which the attempt is recorded as failed","text":"Send-reminder endpoint response time including the provider call (d3 reading)."},{"id":"NFR-6","metric":"≥ 99% of valid bounce webhook events reflected in the reminder history status within 60 s of receipt","text":"Bounce reports from the provider show up in reminder history soon after they arrive."},{"id":"NFR-7","metric":"0 occurrences of customer email addresses in application log output during a full run of the acceptance test suite","text":"Customer email addresses (PII) are not written to application logs."},{"id":"NFR-8","metric":"0 reminder history rows deleted or overwritten by the application, other than the status/reason update from a bounce; rows kept for at least 7 years","text":"Every reminder attempt is kept for audit."},{"id":"NFR-9","metric":"0 duplicate provider send calls when 10 concurrent requests for the same invoice arrive within 1 s","text":"No duplicate emails come from double submits."}],"outOfScope":["Payments and recording payments or marking invoices paid (invoices leave the list only through the paid/closed status already in the invoice data)","Customer logins or any customer-facing screens","SMS reminders","Automatic or scheduled reminders that no staff user triggers","Saving or writing an overdue flag/status on invoice records","More than one email address per customer, or choosing a recipient","Role-based permissions beyond 'any authenticated staff user'","Editing the email template from the UI (template is stored in config)","Creating or editing invoices and customer records, including customer email addresses"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"threshold is 7, business timezone is UTC, today is 2026-09-08, and an open invoice INV-1 has due date 2026-09-01","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"the response is 200 and contains INV-1","when":"GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token"},{"given":"threshold is 7, business timezone is UTC, today is 2026-09-07, and an open invoice INV-2 has due date 2026-09-01 (6 days past due)","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"the response does not contain INV-2","when":"GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token"},{"given":"business timezone is UTC+2, the current UTC time is 2026-09-07T23:30Z (local date 2026-09-08), threshold is 7, and an open invoice INV-3 has due date 2026-09-01","id":"AC-1.3","level":"api","then":"the response contains INV-3","when":"GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token"},{"given":"the overdue threshold setting is changed to 10 and today is 2026-10-15","id":"AC-1.4","level":"api","then":"an open invoice due 2026-10-05 is included and an open invoice due 2026-10-06 is not","when":"the overdue list is requested"}],"ears":"When an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list, the invoice reminders API shall return every invoice that is not paid or closed and for which today's date in the configured business timezone is on or after its due date plus the configured overdue threshold (default 7 days).","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-2","Q-6","ASM-1","ASM-2","ASM-3","ASM-9"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"invoice C is 30 days past its due date with status paid and invoice D is 30 days past its due date with status closed","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"neither C nor D is in the response","when":"GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token"},{"given":"invoice INV-6 is in the overdue list and its status is then changed to paid or closed in the invoice data","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"INV-6 is no longer in the response, with no other action needed","when":"the overdue list is requested again"}],"ears":"If an invoice has a paid or closed status in the existing invoice data, then the invoice reminders API shall leave it out of the overdue list whatever its due date.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-4","ASM-1"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a snapshot of all invoice rows in Postgres is taken, and some of those invoices are overdue","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"every invoice row is byte-for-byte unchanged compared with the snapshot (no status or updated-at column written)","when":"the overdue list endpoint and the invoice detail endpoint for 